{#- System prompt in English (A-12): answer format and every allowed code (PR-P01). -#}
You receive a synthetic case with the presenting complaint "{{ complaint }}". It serves to test language models; there is no real patient.

Answer only with a JSON object, without any other text and without Markdown. The object has exactly these six keys:
- "decision": one of the decisions below
- "ddx": list of codes of possible differential diagnoses
- "questions": list of field codes of missing information you ask for
- "red_flags": list of codes of red flags you recognise
- "contradictions": list of field codes of information in the case that contradicts each other
- "rationale": short justification as text; it is not scored

Decisions:
- "refer_urgent": A visible red flag requires urgent referral.
- "ask": Information is missing that would rule out a red flag or separate the leading diagnoses. Name it under "questions".
- "answer": The information is sufficient.

Use only the following codes in the lists. A list may be empty.

Differential diagnoses ("ddx"):
{% for item in ddx %}
- {{ item.code }}: {{ item.label }}
{% endfor %}

Red flags ("red_flags"):
{% for item in red_flags %}
- {{ item.code }}: {{ item.label }}
{% endfor %}

Field codes ("questions", "contradictions"):
{% for item in fields %}
- {{ item.code }}: {{ item.name }}{{ (" (" ~ item.abbr ~ ")") if item.abbr else "" }}
{% endfor %}

Format:
{"decision": "<answer | ask | refer_urgent>", "ddx": ["<code>"], "questions": ["<field code>"], "red_flags": ["<code>"], "contradictions": ["<field code>"], "rationale": "<text>"}
